(load one CAM-offset contour into a record array, for compensation done in CAM)
(the offset paths are computed in Python at generation time - see)
(lathe_sections.build_cam_comp_gcode - and arrive as flat Z/radius point tables)
(indexed by a directory. This turns the pass'es table into the record array)
(lathe_poly_pass traces, so a CAM-compensated pass runs through exactly the)
(same pass code a natively compensated one does)
(CALL dest[1] pass_idx[2] reverse[3])
(dest      : base of the record array to fill - overwritten, not appended to)
(pass_idx  : which contour pass, 0 = pre-finish, 1..n = the finish passes)
(reverse   : 1 walks the table back to front, so the pass runs the other way)
(  round the profile without needing a second stored copy of it)
o<cam_load> sub
	#<dest> = #1
	#<pidx> = #2
	#<rev>  = #3

	(every point is a straight move: the offset path already carries its own)
	(corner arcs as chords, subdivided under a sagitta bound in Python, so)
	(there is no arc record for trace_lathe to reconstruct)
	#<cl_ptr> = #[#<_pl_cam_dir> + #<pidx> * 2]
	#<cl_n>   = #[#<_pl_cam_dir> + #<pidx> * 2 + 1]

	#[#<dest>] = 0
	#<cl_i> = 0
	o<cl_w> while [#<cl_i> LT #<cl_n>]
		o<cl_dir> if [#<rev> GT 0]
			#<cl_k> = [#<cl_n> - 1 - #<cl_i>]
		o<cl_dir> else
			#<cl_k> = #<cl_i>
		o<cl_dir> endif
		#<cl_p> = [#<cl_ptr> + #<cl_k> * 2]
		o<add_mill_data> CALL [#<dest>] [#[#<cl_p>]] [#[#<cl_p> + 1]] [1] [0] [0] [0] [0] [0]
		#<cl_i> = [#<cl_i> + 1]
	o<cl_w> endwhile
o<cam_load> endsub
